    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12030": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Success",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Assistant Director of Student Success Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director of Student Success Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Assistant Director of Student Success Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Student Success Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Position Summary The Assistant Director of Student Success serves as an operational leader for the Student Success team within Enrollment Management and provides oversight for daily coordination, implementation, and assessment of student success initiatives, student support services, and retention-related operations. At the direction of the Director of Student Success this position provides supervision and leadership to a team of Student Success Specialists while serving as a primary operational liaison between Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, Athletics, Academic Affairs, and other campus partners to ensure students receive coordinated, proactive, and student-centered support throughout their educational journey. The Assistant Director is responsible for managing day-to-day student success operations, coordinating student intervention efforts, monitoring outreach and engagement initiatives, overseeing student support workflows, and assisting with institutional retention efforts using data, technology platforms, and collaborative strategies. This position plays a key role in supporting institutional enrollment, persistence, retention, and student success goals while ensuring operational consistency, accountability, and high-quality student service delivery. The Director of Student Success may alter duties and responsibilities as necessary. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Student Success Operations & Leadership • Oversee the daily operations of the Student Success area within Enrollment Management. • Coordinate and manage frontline student support operations and service delivery within the Turley Center. • Ensure students receive prompt, accurate, and student-centered support related to enrollment, financial aid, student accounts, housing, registration, retention, and student success services. • Assist in the implementation and execution of institutional retention and persistence initiatives. • Monitor operational effectiveness and identify opportunities for process improvement and enhanced student support. • Assist with development and implementation of operational procedures, communication workflows, and student engagement strategies. • Coordinate student outreach and intervention efforts related to retention, persistence, registration, and student success campaigns. • Support divisional and institutional enrollment management initiatives as assigned. • Serve as backup support for safe management and cashiering operations, including opening and closing sessions, balancing daily receipts, and ensuring funds are secured in accordance with university policies and internal controls. Assist in monitoring compliance with cash handling procedures, maintaining accurate records, and escalating discrepancies as needed. • Maintain proper documentation of cash transactions and report any discrepancies in accordance with departmental policy. Supervision & Staff Management • Provide direct supervision, leadership, training, and operational oversight to Student Success Specialists and assigned student employees. • Coordinate staff schedules, office coverage, and operational workflows to ensure consistent student support and service delivery. • Conduct onboarding and training for new staff members related to university systems, customer service expectations, operational procedures, and student support protocols. • Monitor staff performance, productivity, documentation, responsiveness, and adherence to institutional expectations and operational procedures. • Assist with performance evaluations, coaching, professional development, and corrective action documentation as appropriate. • Foster a collaborative, student-centered, and solutions-oriented team of culture. Student Support, Outreach & Intervention • Provide leadership, coordination, and accountability for Student Success Specialists and support staff in advancing institutional retention and persistence goals. • Ensure Specialists actively contribute toward divisional and university retention objectives through proactive outreach, student engagement, intervention efforts, and coordinated student support initiatives. • Collaborate with the Director of Student Success to monitor retention progress, identify barriers impacting persistence, and implement operational strategies that support overall student retention and success. • Coordinate proactive student outreach efforts related to: o Registration o Academic progress o Early alerts o Student account concerns o Financial aid follow-up o Enrollment persistence o Retention campaigns • Assist the Director in managing student intervention strategies for at-risk students through coordinated support efforts and referrals. • Serve as an escalation point for complex student concerns requiring other coordination or support. • Coordinate referrals between Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, CARE Team representatives, and other campus resources. • Assist with orientation, welcome programming, commencement activities, Maroon & White events, and other enrollment and retention-related initiatives. Technology & Reporting • Lead with operational oversight and utilization of Navigate360/Slate and other student success technologies, serving as a SuperUser representative for the Enrollment Management Division with operational oversight and utilization of Navigate360/Slate and other student success technologies. • Monitor and ensure appropriate documentation standards and utilization expectations within Navigate360/Slate. • Provide regular reports to the Director on efficacy of outreach and campaigns and any other pertinent information related to retention. • Assist with development and execution of student success campaigns, appointment campaigns, early alerts, and retention initiatives within Navigate360/Slate. • Utilize institutional data, reporting tools, and student success technologies to monitor outreach effectiveness, identify trends, and support operational decision-making. • Collaborate with Institutional Research, Information Technology, and campus stakeholders to improve student success reporting and intervention processes. Minimum Required Education Minimum of a Bachelor’s Degree in Education, Business Administration, Psychology in a related field. Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Minimum of three (3) years of progressive experience in student services, enrollment management, student success, retention, advising, or related higher education operations. Demonstrated experience coordinating student support services and managing operational workflows. Experience supervising staff, student employees, or teams. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Experience using student information systems, CRM platforms, or student success technologies. Ability to analyze information, solve problems, and make sound operational decisions. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, Leadership, or related field. Experience utilizing Navigate360, Banner, Slate, TouchNet, or related higher education systems. Experience with student retention initiatives, early alert systems, and student intervention models. Experience working collaboratively across academic and student support units. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027015SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/19/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11756 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12060": {
      "title": "Events and Facilities Operations Worker",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Events and Facilities Operations Worker Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Events and Facilities Operations Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Events and Facilities Operations Worker Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Facilities - Grounds Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Fairmont State University is seeking a dependable, safety-conscious, and service-oriented individual to join our Facilities team. This position plays an important role in supporting daily campus operations, university events, and the overall appearance, safety, and functionality of our campus. Performs a variety of hands-on duties, including event setup and breakdown, furniture and equipment relocation, groundskeeping, snow and ice removal, sanitation, material transportation, and general facilities support. The successful candidate will operate a variety of vehicles, tools, and equipment and work collaboratively with university departments to support campus activities and special events. This position requires flexibility, physical stamina, a commitment to safety, and the ability to respond to changing operational needs, including inclement weather and occasional mandatory overtime. If you enjoy working in a team-oriented environment and take pride in helping maintain a welcoming, safe, and well-functioning campus, we encourage you to apply and become part of the Fairmont State University community. Incumbent will support all university events through set-ups, tear downs, loading and moving of needed material and equipment including tables, chairs, tents, benches, etc. Relocates offices and classrooms within buildings and throughout campus by lifting, loading and unloading furniture, filing cabinets, boxes, etc. onto hand trucks, dollies, and box vans for transportation. May require removing desk components, doors, and shelves to ease in relocations. Moves, sets-up, rearranges, and erects tables, chairs, platforms, bleachers, tents, displays, etc. May assist in the design for special event set-ups. Reads floor plans and layouts for concerts, registration, commencement, and other special statewide University affiliated events. Drives box vans, forklifts, front loaders, small dump trucks, and operates lift gates. Operates, maintains, and services equipment and tools that are used while performing moves, set-ups, sanitation services, and snow removal. Operates motor vehicle (i.e. car, box van, pick-up truck, fork lift, front loader, small dump truck…) to transport people, to deliver/receive surplus for inventory control, to deliver, receive, or remove surplus materials for shops and equipment throughout the campus and community and statewide. Unloads and stores supplies, rotating stock and equipment at various job sites. Establishes and maintains inventory of departments throughout institutional buildings, warehouse, or stockroom on equipment e.g. tables, chairs, tents, staging, platforms. Collects and properly disposes of trash and litter throughout institutional buildings and grounds, including cleaning of trash receptacles and assisting sanitation vehicles operators. Collects and properly stores hazardous materials, e.g. muriatic acid, propane, diesel fuel, anti-freeze, chlorine, alcohol, and sodium bi-carbonate. At time of inclement weather or as directed by Facilities administration, will work as required to removes snow from sidewalks, steps, roads, and parking lots using hand tools, power brooms, and snow blowers. Spreads de-icers and limestone chips on all areas as needed. Removes graffiti from walls and sidewalks; performs all outside cleaning activities as required. Operates high-pressure washers, sandblasters, and other power equipment to complete these tasks. Operates blowers and walk-behind sweepers to clean and remove debris in maintaining the appearance of institutional grounds. As assigned, assists with landscape construction by: operating jackhammers and other related equipment to remove broken sidewalks; mixing, pouring, and spreading concrete, asphalt, gravel, and other materials; digs holes and trenches to assist in the repair or replacement of utility lines, irrigation and drainage systems by using hand and power tools; excavates and prepares grounds prior to initiation of construction projects. As needed, will be required to maintain and care for institutional grounds by mowing, trimming and edging around trees, flower beds, buildings, and walkways; watering lawns, shrubs, and ornamental gardens during dry periods. Removes weeds from flowers, shrubs, and ground cover as required. Removing and disposing of debris throughout grounds area. Collects recyclable items and places in appropriate storage location. Must be able to provide support to academics, special events for Fairmont State University campus community and throughout the state, which requires flexible hours and mandatory overtime. As needed, assists in preparing grounds and ornamental beds for planting and seeding, hauls and spreads topsoil and mixed in fertilizer, peat moss, compost vermiculite, and other additives to condition the soil. Assists in planting ornamentals, flowers, shrubs, and trees as required. As needed, operates, services, and maintains hand power tools and equipment such as weed-eaters, lawn mowers, roto-tillers, walk-behind sweepers, and vacs. Positions are considered essential and should plan to work during inclement weather or snow events. Positions could be assigned to work non-standard hours as required. May be required to perform various maintenance tasks either assisting or under the direction of qualified craft persons (plumbing, carpentry, painting, etc.). These tasks would be considered non-technical, non-certified, supporting duties. Attends various training classes, seminars, and other meetings to learn new techniques and procedures and to remain current in all safety requirements. Must be able to respond to emergency situations and events, which include snow removal. Minimum Required Education High School Diploma or GED Required Licenses and/or Certifications West Virginia Driver’s License Minimum Required Qualifications Ability to perform physically demanding outdoor work in various weather conditions. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong work ethic and reliability. Knowledge of landscaping practices and grounds maintenance. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and perform repetitive physical tasks. Good communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ability and capability to perform essential job functions. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027034SP Number of Vacancies 3 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Job Close Date 11/04/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12058 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12028": {
      "title": "Financial Reporting Manager",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Financial Reporting Manager Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Financial Reporting Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Financial Reporting Manager Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Accounting Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Financial Reporting Manager supports the financial operations of Fairmont State University by collecting, reviewing and analyzing financial data for external and internal financial reporting requirements. This role assists in producing timely, accurate and compliant financial reports while adhering to federal, state and institutional regulations and guidelines, maintains strong communication and relationships with the campus community and key financial stakeholders. Operational Duties: Internal Reporting – Assist with monthly, quarterly and year-end closing activities, including but not limited to preparing accrual entries, completing, reviewing and correcting journal entries, account reconciliations, and financial data to ensure the accuracy of financial information Collect interim financial data, identify significant variances, interpret data, and collaborate with the Finance team to compile monthly financial statements Create regular, recurring and ad hoc internal reports as needed to support university-wide decision-making Internal reporting includes but is not limited to financial statements, capital project budget reports, fixed asset reports and proformas External Reporting – Collaborate with Institutional Resources to complete all required and requested external reporting in compliance with state, federal and higher education reporting requirements for various third-party stakeholders External reporting includes but is not limited to Internal Revenue Service ( IRS ), National Collegiate Athletic Association ( NCAA ), Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System ( IPEDS ), Higher Education Policy Commission ( HEPC ) and the State of West Virginia. Audit Coordination – Assist Finance leaders with the preparation of the University’s annual audited consolidated financial statements, ensuring accuracy and compliance with policies, federal and state laws, Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and Governmental Accounting Standards Board ( GASB ) standards. Duties include but are not limited to developing workpapers, preparing schedules, creating and reviewing journal entries and collecting documentation. Audits include but are not limited to National Collegiate Athletic Association ( NCAA ), Research & Development (R&D) and Single Financial Audit ( SFA ) Process Improvement & Systems Optimization: Policy Development: Work with Finance team to evaluate, update, implement and document departmental and university-wide financial policies and procedures. Unit Collaboration: Collaboration includes but is not limited to, partnering with the Finance Team to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting and to ensure alignment between budget and actual reporting; and collaborating with departments across the university to promote clear understanding of financial data and processes Improvement: Drive continuous improvement by automating manual processes and enhancing ERP system functionality in conjunction with the State of WV’s ERP system Other: Participates in other projects and performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related business field (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications 3-5 years prior experience with Finance, Accounting or Budgets, however, any equivalent combination of education and/or experience is acceptable which provides an applicant with the listed knowledge, skills, abilities and capability to perform the essential functions of the job High attention to detail and strong written and verbal communication skills Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel (including formulas, data sorting, and pivot tables). Strict ethical standards for handling data confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Experience with higher education finances Experience with annual audit coordination Strong understanding of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ) and Governmental Accounting Standard Board ( GASB ) Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027017SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/20/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11768 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12038": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant and Project Manager– Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Executive Assistant and Project Manager– Enrollment Management Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Executive Assistant and Project Manager– Enrollment Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Executive Assistant and Project Manager– Enrollment Management Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Enrollment Management Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Executive Assistant and Project Manager, provides high-level executive, financial, operational, and project management support to the Vice President of Enrollment Management and the Enrollment Management leadership team. Serving as a key operational partner within the division, this position coordinates strategic initiatives, manages divisional projects and timelines, supports budget planning and financial operations, and helps ensure priorities move effectively from planning through implementation. The position works collaboratively across Enrollment Management and with University partners to coordinate complex and cross-functional projects, establish timelines and deliverables, monitor progress, identify barriers, facilitate communication, and provide regular updates to leadership. The position also manages and coordinates divisional budget and procurement activities, executive scheduling for the VP and AVP , communications, travel, personnel processes, and other administrative operations. The successful candidate must demonstrate strong judgment, initiative, organization, discretion, problem-solving skills, and the ability to independently manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Executive and Leadership Support Provide high-level executive and administrative support to the Vice President of Enrollment Management and support the Enrollment Management leadership team as appropriate. Manage the Vice President’s calendar, meetings, appointments, priorities, and scheduling needs. Coordinate meeting logistics, develop agendas and materials, document decisions and action items, and monitor necessary follow-up. Prepare and edit executive correspondence, reports, presentations, briefing materials, and other communications. Coordinate travel arrangements, itineraries, registrations, and related logistics for the Vice President and Enrollment Management leadership as assigned. Serve as a primary point of coordination between the Office of the Vice President, Enrollment Management departments, University leadership, campus partners, and external stakeholders. Exercise discretion and sound judgment when managing confidential, sensitive, or time-critical information. Anticipate needs, identify issues requiring attention, gather necessary information, and assist in developing solutions before matters are escalated to the Vice President. Assist with divisional personnel processes, including full-time hires, temporary appointments, graduate assistants, onboarding, and related administrative needs. Provide coordination and administrative support for Enrollment Management leadership meetings, retreats, planning sessions, and other divisional activities. Budget, Finance, and Procurement Coordinate divisional budget development and ongoing budget management in collaboration with the Vice President, Enrollment Management leadership, Finance, and departmental budget managers. Maintain comprehensive oversight of Enrollment Management budgets, expenditures, commitments, and available resources and provide regular financial updates to leadership. Monitor spending and identify potential budget concerns, resource needs, efficiencies, and opportunities for strategic reallocation. Coordinate regular budget reviews with departmental budget managers to evaluate expenditures, projections, priorities, and resource needs. Manage divisional procurement processes and ensure compliance with University purchasing and financial policies. Coordinate requisitions, purchase orders, vendor documentation, payment processing, purchasing-card activity, and other procurement functions as assigned. Serve as a resource to Enrollment Management staff regarding purchasing, travel, reimbursement, and other divisional financial processes. Coordinate expense reporting and reimbursement processes for designated Enrollment Management employees. Maintain appropriate financial documentation and support reconciliation, reporting, audit, and year-end processes. Collaborate with Finance and Procurement to resolve financial or purchasing issues affecting divisional operations. Project Management and Strategic Initiatives Manage and coordinate strategic projects and initiatives on behalf of the Vice President and Enrollment Management leadership team from initiation through completion. Develop project plans identifying objectives, scope, deliverables, milestones, timelines, responsible parties, dependencies, and anticipated outcomes. Maintain a centralized portfolio of Enrollment Management projects and priorities to provide leadership with visibility into project status, deadlines, outstanding decisions, risks, and next steps. Facilitate cross-functional project meetings and ensure decisions, responsibilities, action items, and deadlines are clearly documented and communicated. Monitor project progress and proactively follow up with responsible individuals and teams to support timely completion of deliverables. Identify project delays, barriers, competing priorities, dependencies, or resource needs and elevate issues requiring leadership attention. Coordinate initiatives involving multiple Enrollment Management units and University partners, establishing clear ownership and facilitating communication across functional areas. Develop and maintain project dashboards, trackers, implementation plans, status reports, executive summaries, presentations, and other project-management tools. Assist leadership with post-project assessment to identify outcomes, lessons learned, unresolved items, and opportunities for continuous improvement. Divisional Operations and Communication Help coordinate operational priorities across Enrollment Management and facilitate communication among divisional departments. Maintain divisional calendars, deadlines, planning documents, project trackers, and other tools that support effective coordination and accountability. Assist with preparing and distributing divisional communications, meeting materials, announcements, reports, and presentations. Coordinate information and materials needed for University leadership, institutional committees, meetings, presentations, and other strategic activities. Establish and maintain organized records and documentation for divisional projects, financial operations, contracts, personnel activities, and administrative processes. Evaluate administrative processes and recommend improvements that increase efficiency, consistency, transparency, and service. Support a collaborative, responsive, student-centered culture throughout Enrollment Management. Perform other duties and coordinate special initiatives as assigned by the Vice President or his/her leadership team. Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience. Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Demonstrated experience managing multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines simultaneously. Strong organizational and project coordination skills with demonstrated attention to detail. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, solve problems, and appropriately escalate issues. Experience coordinating work involving multiple departments, stakeholders, or functional areas. Ability to develop and maintain project plans, trackers, timelines, reports, and other organizational tools. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with senior leaders and diverse internal and external stakeholders. Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion. Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office and contemporary collaboration, communication, and productivity technologies. Ability to adapt to changing priorities and operate effectively in a fast-paced environment. Commitment to excellent service and a student-centered University environment. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience in higher education, Enrollment Management, executive administration, business operations, project management, or a related environment. Experience managing or coordinating budgets, procurement, purchasing, or financial operations. Experience coordinating cross-functional projects from planning through implementation. Experience with project-management or collaborative work-management platforms. Experience supporting senior or executive-level leadership. Experience with process improvement, change management, implementation planning, or organizational operations. Project management training or certification. Familiarity with higher education administrative systems, enterprise systems, CRM platforms, or related technology. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027032SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 09/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11966 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
