    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12065": {
      "title": "Director of the Folklife Center",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Director of the Folklife Center Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Director of the Folklife Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Director of the Folklife Center Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Community Programs Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Director of the Folklife Center provides leadership and oversight for the development, coordination, and delivery of folk and traditional arts programming that celebrates and preserves West Virginia’s cultural heritage. This position oversees the Center’s exhibitions, collections, archives, publications, and educational programming while fostering meaningful partnerships with community members, cultural organizations, university departments, and external stakeholders. The Director is responsible for the Center’s daily operations, staff supervision, budget management, fundraising initiatives, and stewardship of its facilities and collections, ensuring that the Center advances its mission through community engagement, scholarship, preservation, and public programming. Duties and Responsibilities: Develops and offers folk and traditional arts programming in collaboration with community members and groups Coordinates and directs the work of student workers and staff in the completion of special projects for the Center’s programming; Oversees curation, creation and installation of changing exhibitions and displays; updates permanent displays as needed; Coordinates with staff to oversee archival research and scholarly inquiries; Writes, edits, and publishes related folklife/folklore works on behalf of and for the Center, including press releases, exhibition text, website copy, social media copy, and more; Oversees the publication of Traditions, the annual WV folklore journal; Recommends and manages all protocol and programmatic policies; Oversees budget development and monitoring for the Center and ensures careful stewardship of the Center’s financial and physical assets; Selects, trains, supervises, and evaluates the professional and administrative staff assigned to the Center Collaborates with other university departments and offices to promote programs, exhibitions, and archives; Seeks out opportunities for community collaboration, engagement, and promotion; Collaborates with the College of Liberal Arts, Office of Sponsored Programs, and Fairmont State Foundation on internal and external fundraising, including grants;: In coordination with physical plant, oversees repairs and maintenance of and plans for enhancements to the Center building and grounds; Coordinates with Folklife Center staff, catering, and physical plant on event set-up; Oversees the archiving and curation of the Center’s collections; Oversees proper storage of the Center’s collections; Works with the advisory committee toward creating a quality collection that best embodies the Center’s mission statement; Oversees equipment, supplies, and materials: ensures that equipment is functional and that supplies and materials used in classes, workshops, collections management, exhibitions, and Folklife Center programs are sufficient. Works with other campus stakeholders to coordinate programming and events. Minimum Required Education A Bachelor’s Degree or higher in museum management, history, folklore, or a related field. Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications Demonstrated experience in program development and facilities management. Preferred Qualifications A Master’s Degree or higher in museum management, history, folklore, or a related field. A track record of leadership and experience coordinating and fundraising with local community groups. Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027035SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Job Close Date 11/04/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12063 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12094": {
      "title": "Academic Success Coordinator for Recruitment",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Academic Success Coordinator for Recruitment Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academic Success Coordinator for Recruitment Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Academic Success Coordinator for Recruitment Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department College of Liberal Arts Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Fairmont State University is seeking an organized, student-focused Academic Advisor for Recruitment to support the College of Liberal Arts. This position plays an important role in welcoming new students, supporting recruitment and onboarding efforts, coordinating new student orientation, and providing academic advising and registration assistance. Working collaboratively with faculty, Admissions, and campus partners, the Academic Advisor for Recruitment will help students navigate university processes, understand academic policies, and successfully transition into their college experience. The ideal candidate is committed to student success, relationship-building, and supporting enrollment and retention initiatives. Position Description Under the supervision of the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts and in close collaboration with the Academic Advisor for Retention, the Academic Advisor for Recruitment will serve as the key point of contact for recruitment and onboarding of new students for the College of Liberal Arts. Administrative and Operational Support Admissions Team Liaison (working with Admissions and Welcome Center) to ensure excellent on-boarding experience and service for new students Attends on-campus recruitment events such as Day on Campus and Maroon and White Day Travels to designated off-campus recruitments events Assist with advising and registration of Dual Enrollment students Oversee designing, ordering, and maintaining college wide and program specific recruitment and materials and resources Create and maintain Dual Enrollment communication plan for students and faculty Maintain strong working relationships with various departments across campus Provide general support for enrollment, retention, and engagement efforts within College of Liberal Arts Assist with processing advising forms for students Student Programming Main point of contact for all new students to College of Liberal Arts Planning and executing New Student Orientations including academic presentation and registration process Advise all new students for the college each term and assist students in registering for classes through individual advising appointments and group registration sessions Serve as backup advisor for all faculty advisors in the College of Liberal Arts in times of need (Summer break, Orientations, Faculty out of office, and peak registration times) Informs students of academic policies and procedures for class registration, degree requirements, course replacement/withdraw, and academic warning/probation/suspension Other duties as assigned Minimum Required Education Master’s Degree, preferably in Higher Education or related field Required Licenses and/or Certifications Valid Driver’s License Minimum Required Qualifications Strong interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Proficient in Microsoft Office Preferred Qualifications Experience working in Academic Affairs Experience in Degreeworks, Slate, and Banner At least one (1) year of experience in academic advising, counseling, or student support services Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027038SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/28/2026 Job Close Date 11/11/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12092 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
