    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12132": {
      "title": "Manager of Grant Financial Operations",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Manager of Grant Financial Operations Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Manager of Grant Financial Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Manager of Grant Financial Operations Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Accounting Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The Manager of Grant Financial Operations supports the fiscal administration and financial compliance of Fairmont State University’s sponsored programs including federal, state and private grants, contracts and awards. This role provides grant financial data to key stakeholders including but not limited to leadership, the Office of Sponsored Programs, Principal Investigators and all granting agencies/partners as required or requested Operational Duties Manages the creation and closure of restricted funds within the University’s chart of accounts Maintains restricted funds by tracking expenses, allocating payroll, updating budgets, posting journal entries and performs budget-to-actual reconciliations for receipts and disbursements Prevents or corrects improper cost transfers and posting errors. Completes month-end processes for restricted funds and runs monthly financial reports and schedules Ensures a positive cash flow for restricted funds which includes but is not limited to timely invoices, completion of draw requests and required grant reporting Collaborates with Finance areas and Human Resources to create, calculate and balance grant funded positions Assists with the development of a streamlined cross-institutional billing workflow with Fairmont State Foundation Works directly with Fairmont State Foundation to invoice for reimbursements and reconcile grant funded requests Audit and Reporting Assists with year-end processes and audit functions for the annual financial audit, including but not limited to timing functions to prepare schedules, completing calculation and analysis, creating and posting accrual entries and providing support documentation as requested by the auditors for restricted funds Primary point of contact and coordinator for Research and Development audits Ensures compliance with all financial reporting obligations Assists with the completion of annual requirements for restricted funds including but not limited to Expenditure Schedule, Schedule of Expenditures of Federal Awards ( SEFA ) and Appropriation Requests for the State of West Virginia Process Improvement & Systems Optimization Policy Development: Work with Finance team to evaluate, update, implement and document departmental and university-wide financial policies and procedures. Unit Collaboration: Collaboration includes but is not limited to, partnering with the Finance Team to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting and to ensure alignment between budget and actual reporting; and collaborating with departments across the university to promote clear understanding of financial data and processes Improvement: Drive continuous improvement by automating manual processes and enhancing ERP system functionality in conjunction with the State of WV’s ERP system Other Participates in other projects and performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration or a related business field (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Required Licenses and/or Certifications N/A Minimum Required Qualifications 2-4 years prior experience with Finance, Accounting or Budgets, however, any equivalent combination of education and/or experience is acceptable which provides an applicant with the listed knowledge, skills, abilities and capability to perform the essential functions of the job High attention to detail and strong written and verbal communication skills Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel (including formulas, data sorting, and pivot tables). Strict ethical standards for handling data confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Experience with federal, state, local, or private grant administration Strong understanding of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ), Governmental Accounting Standard Board ( GASB ) and Uniform Guidance rules Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027013SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/19/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11751 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12131": {
      "title": "Enrollment Systems Specialist",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Enrollment Systems Specialist Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Enrollment Systems Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Enrollment Systems Specialist Type of Position Staff - Full Time Department Enrollment Services Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours NA F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Director of Enrollment Technology and Operations, the Enrollment Systems Specialist will be an expert in the use and optimization of the Slate CRM and related systems to support the successful business operations of the Enrollment Management division and the mission and goals of the University. This position is required to work on campus a minimum of four days per week. The remaining workday may be completed remotely, subject to departmental needs and supervisor approval. Duties and Responsibilities: Configure, maintain, and troubleshoot enrollment management CRM software. Ensure CRM data integrity by implementing and requiring data standards and uniformity. Ensure adherence to federal and institutional data privacy regulations and policies. Perform daily de-duplication and cleansing of CRM person and organization data. Manage CRM end-users to include development of roles and permissions that follows industry best practices for minimum amount of access to support successful completion of job duties. Be an enrollment management data expert to support accurate creation and maintenance of CRM data queries and reports. Ensure alignment of data collection and categorization across the CRM and student information system. Evaluate current and future Enrollment Management business process operations needs and identify how the CRM can be used to provide the most optimal and productive operational outcomes. Recommend and implement business process workflows. Provide daily operational support to Slate end-users via service management software to include triaging and resolution of issues. Partner with central IT teams to build and maintain data interfaces between Slate and other University systems as well as with external partners. Perform data uploads, monitor automations, and manage error handling. Document all aspects of the CRM related to system administration and data interfacing. Create and maintain knowledge base articles related to the functional use of the CRM . Collaborate with and support departments like Admissions, Financial Aid, IT, and the academic colleges and schools in the effective use of the CRM to improve business strategies and attain enrollment goals. Utilize programming languages like SQL , HTML , CSS , and JavaScript for system customization. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Required Education Bachelor’s Degree. Required Licenses and/or Certifications Valid Driver’s License. Minimum Required Qualifications Experience in administering technology in a higher education setting. Knowledge of higher education policy and practices. Experience administering and utilizing CRM software. Experience managing database records and ensuring data integrity to include compliance with data privacy policies. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Slate Technolutions CRM Software Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027020SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11785 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
