    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12195": {
      "title": "Library Technical Assistant I",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Library Technical Assistant I Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Library Technical Assistant I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Library Technical Assistant I Type of Position Staff - Part Time Department Library Services Appointment Length July - June (12 mo) Benefits Eligible? No Published Salary Requested Part-Time Staff Hours 950 F.T.E. 0.49 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities The duties will include, but are not limited to: circulation of library materials; staffing and supporting library programming; handling of funds for printing, copying, and faxing; assistance to library users in the location of materials and provision of information; instruction in the process of adding Falcon dollars and printing; support in the use of library technology. Duties also include shelving of library materials and general maintenance of library collection. This position requires employee to work a flexible schedule day/evening/nights and weekends. Minimum Required Education High school education plus up to six months experience is acceptable, which provides an applicant the listed knowledge, skills, and abilities and the capability to perform the essential functions of the job. Required Licenses and/or Certifications Knowledge of automated library circulation systems, preferably OCLC WorldShare. Minimum Required Qualifications Proven ability to work effectively and efficiently with students, faculty and other patrons in an academic library setting. Proven ability and skill in multitasking effectively, handling several requests and situations at once, resolving them quickly and efficiently. Proven initiative and the ability to think proactively, analytically and strategically, to anticipate and act on the needs of patrons and other aspects of improved and enhanced library services. Strong customer skills, especially in the arenas of providing swift and efficient services and serving many customers in a short period but with professionalism and courtesy. Proven ability to maintain high level of confidentiality with faculty, staff, students and co-workers. Ability to deal calmly and appropriately with on-shift emergencies, notify appropriate staff and handle according to established procedures. Preferred Qualifications NA Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2027042SP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 11/20/2026 Job Close Date 12/04/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/12193 Job Duties Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
